From 1be99e788e8533524ce2c41636a20b80ca5a13bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lonkwitz <mawelo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:16:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] [AI generated] AIX: build system (CMake, presets, IBM
 Open XL toolchain files, Makefile), README section

* CMakeLists.txt: AIX branch (sources, -D_ALL_SOURCE -D_THREAD_SAFE,
  -lperfstat), no -fstack-clash-protection on AIX, and BTOP_GIT_COMMIT to embed
  the commit in --version when building from a tarball without .git.
* CMakePresets.json: aix-openxl (AIX 7.2 TL5+/7.3, IBM Open XL C/C++ 17.1.3,
  64-bit), aix-openxl-debug, aix71-openxl and aix61-openxl (build on a 7.2 host
  against a sysroot of the target release with a static libc++ 19, see
  tools/aix/sysroot71).
* cmake/Toolchain-aix-openxl.cmake and cmake/Toolchain-aix-sysroot-openxl.cmake.
  Both set the library search path of the binary to /usr/lib:/lib. Otherwise
  CMake writes directories of the build host into the loader section (for the
  sysroot builds the sysroot and runtime directories), and the loader on the
  target host searches them first.
* Makefile: platform aix (gmake, no LTO), sources via $(wildcard) because AIX
  find has no -maxdepth.
* README.md: section "Compilation AIX".
* docs/aix: how to build for AIX 7.1 and 6.1, why that needs a sysroot and a
  static libc++, and the AIX pitfalls met while porting (reference).
